# Copy to runner-env.local for unattended local runs when the background runner
# needs a deterministic environment that differs from your interactive shell.
#
# Keep runner-env.local out of version control. Common uses:
# - API-key auth for Codex or Claude when login state is not visible in background services
# - explicit PATH or HOME for launchd or systemd user services
# - user-specific config roots such as XDG_CONFIG_HOME or CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY=replace-me-if-needed
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=replace-me-if-needed
# HOME=/Users/your-user
# PATH=/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
# XDG_CONFIG_HOME=/Users/your-user/.config
# NVM_DIR=/Users/your-user/.nvm
# Avoid setting CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR unless you intentionally use a non-default Claude config root
# and have verified `claude auth status` still works with that override.
